  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A beam of monochromatic light is used to excite the electron in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;from the first orbit to the third orbit. The wavelength of monochromatic light is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p>[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1242</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "114",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Energy released in the transition will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p><p>Now energy of photon can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12400</mn><mrow><mn>108</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mover><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>114</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mover></math></p>",
